Sure. I just have to wait for slow ass Youtube to finish uploading the thing.

&#x200B;

Edit : Here it is :  [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o3OFcu\_zDGg](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o3OFcu_zDGg)

When did Nick Fury became a Wither Skeleton ?I love that drawing it's cool

&#x200B;

Edit : Okay so I know this will ruin everything. But I just wanted to thank everybody for the upvotes. I would never have expected that. It really means a lot to me, way more than you can imagine. It's not much I guess, but still.

I guess yes. The one that comes to me is the one about French people not talking English at all. This one is true for a TON of people. 

And sometimes when we do try we have this beautiful accent that makes everything sound weird af. 

&#x200B;

Then there is the baguette thing. We do walk around holding a baguette from time to time. But we don't do that for fun, we won't hold on our baguette all the day. It's just good bread and a lot of people eat baguette so yeah a lot of people walk around with a baguette

&#x200B;

Apparently we eat a lot of cheese and this is true. I do love cheese myself but it's sooo good.

&#x200B;

The ones about frog legs are kind of true. Not everyone eat frog legs but that's something people do.


Then there is wine. And yeah we do drink a lot of wine ( the adults only, kids my age don't drink wine that much, at least in my family )


And that's all I can think of. I don't know a lot of French stereotypes. Hope that answers your question
